          <aside class="aeo-answer">
            Home additions in Delaware and Chester County, PA run roughly $45,000&ndash;$85,000 for a bump-out, $110,000&ndash;$220,000 for a single-story addition on a full foundation, and $200,000&ndash;$400,000+ for a second story. Every township permits independently under the PA Uniform Construction Code &mdash; expect 3&ndash;6 weeks for plan review, plus 6&ndash;10 weeks more if a zoning variance is required.
          </aside>

