              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="post-body__section post-body__section--from-our-work reveal" aria-label="From Our Work">
              <h2>From Our Work: Foundations Are Where Additions Get Expensive</h2>
              <p>On a bump-out addition in Newtown Square, a soil test we insisted on before pricing revealed the back corner of the lot sat on fill dirt from decades-old grading &mdash; it needed a deeper footing than the rest of the foundation. Skipping that test would have meant a mid-project change order and a homeowner blindsided by cost. We build soil and utility checks into every addition quote now specifically because of jobs like that one.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="post-body__section post-cta reveal">
              <h2>Weighing an Addition in Delaware or Chester County?</h2>
              <p>Additions are one of the few renovations where getting the structural and permitting groundwork right the first time saves real money &mdash; reworking a rejected zoning submission or an under-engineered foundation costs far more than getting it correct up front. Free site visit and realistic scope before any design work begins. 5.0 rating &middot; 135+ projects &middot; PA HIC #195591.</p>
